From 249b8667fa8caf032b8a14980161c09657defeb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:16:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: sparx5: count the DWRR inputs as the hardware does
Organization: Wires

An ets qdisc with weighted bands also weighted the lowest strict
band.  With

    tc qdisc add dev eth0 root handle 1: ets bands 8 strict 4 \
        quanta 4500 4500 500 500

queue 4 shared the port with queues 0 to 3 instead of taking
precedence over them.

SE_DWRR_CNT was written as the number of weighted queues, but the
register counts from one: "0: No inputs uses DWRR, 1: 2 lowest
inputs used DWRR, n: (n+1) lowest inputs uses DWRR", per the LAN969x
register description, and the vendor API subtracts one as well.

Write the count less one, and zero for none.

Signed-off-by: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c
index 14331f1a0c57..7ee5c90f1a79 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c
@@ -394,8 +394,8 @@ static int sparx5_dwrr_conf_set(struct sparx5_port *port,
 		 HSCH_HSCH_CFG_CFG_HSCH_LAYER | HSCH_HSCH_CFG_CFG_CFG_SE_IDX,
 		 port->sparx5, HSCH_HSCH_CFG_CFG);
 
-	/* Number of *lower* indexes that are arbitrated dwrr */
-	spx5_rmw(HSCH_SE_CFG_SE_DWRR_CNT_SET(dwrr->count),
+	/* The inputs 0 to SE_DWRR_CNT are arbitrated dwrr, the rest strict */
+	spx5_rmw(HSCH_SE_CFG_SE_DWRR_CNT_SET(dwrr->count ? dwrr->count - 1 : 0),
 		 HSCH_SE_CFG_SE_DWRR_CNT, port->sparx5,
 		 HSCH_SE_CFG(port->portno));
 
